<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linzi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Linzi was the capital of the State of Qi for most of the Zhou period until its conquest by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 221 BCE, on the site of the modern district of Linzi in Zibo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>. One of the largest cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>, it was famous for its crowded markets, its wealth and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jixia-academy">Jixia Academy</a> of scholars. It was taken by the Yan general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yue-yi">Yue Yi</a> in 284 BCE.</p></div>
